# ============================================================================
# .env.example — environment variable template (retro-shmup)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file lists the environment KEYS the project reads, with placeholder
# values only. It is committed; real dotenv files (.env, .env.local,
# .env.production, ...) are gitignored and never committed.
#
# The project has no secrets in 1.0: it is a static web game with no backend
# (ADR-0006). The only credential involved in delivery is the itch.io butler
# key (BUTLER_API_KEY), not provisioned yet (SECURITY.md), never a file; Cloudflare Pages
# deploys through its GitHub App with no repository-held credential (ADR-0004).
#
# Profile A (static site): the only environment-specific value is the public
# base URL per build target. See the `environments` skill.
# ============================================================================

# Public base path of the build, wired into Vite's `base` option.
# Vite exposes VITE_* variables to the browser bundle — never put a secret here.
# Default './' (relative): the same build works at the Cloudflare Pages root and
# inside itch.io's embedded player, which serves from a sub-path (ADR-0004).
# VITE_BASE_URL=./

# The feedback form's address (GDD v0.26 §9.1, ADR-0027): a public Tally form,
# opened in a new tab. Empty or unset hides every feedback entry point; any value
# not starting with https://tally.so/ fails the build.
# VITE_FEEDBACK_FORM_URL=https://tally.so/r/FORM_ID

# The online leaderboard's origin (ADR-0031 decision 12): a bare https:// origin,
# no path. Set only in the production Pages environment; the feature is built in
# only when package.json holds a strict X.Y.Z above 0.0.0 and RELEASE_COMMIT
# (a Pages variable set by the release procedure) equals CF_PAGES_COMMIT_SHA.
# Otherwise it is off; any other address fails the build.
# VITE_LEADERBOARD_URL=https://leaderboard.example
# RELEASE_COMMIT=<full SHA of the tagged release commit>
